3167..3238 Comment "/// Spinning a sum is composing the spins (cubical\'s `intLoop-hom`), by"
3239..3312 Comment "/// induction on the second summand. `spin` puts its new loop first where"
3313..3390 Comment "/// cubical\'s `intLoop` puts it last, so the law composes the spins the other"
3391..3452 Comment "/// way round, as the words compute: `(loop ∷ p) then q` is"
3453..3530 Comment "/// `loop ∷ (p then q)`. At zero `spin(Z)` is a call that returns the empty"
3531..3588 Comment "/// word, and the composite over it runs that call first."
